message: "If you use SeqChem, please cite this software."
title: "SeqChem: free chemistry and bioinformatics web tools and JSON API"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "SeqChem contributors"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24310592"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24310591"
    description: "Concept DOI for all versions"
url: "https://seqandchem.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MR820/seqandchem"
repository-artifact: "https://zenodo.org/records/24310592"
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  SeqChem is a free web application and JSON API for chemistry and
  bioinformatics. It converts 190+ chemical formats (SMILES, InChI, MOL, SDF,
  PDB, MOL2, XYZ, CML), calculates molecular properties, draws 2D structures,
  generates 3D conformers, runs SMARTS substructure and Tanimoto similarity
  searches, resolves IUPAC names, and processes FASTA/FASTQ sequences. No
  account or API key is required.
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - bioinformatics
  - SMILES
  - InChI
  - structure conversion
  - FASTA
  - FASTQ
  - OpenBabel
  - JSON API
